David Weis <davidw@yang.earlham.edu> writes:

> How do you get more than one pet?

Peter Snelling responds:

> 1 - If you see a stray dog/cat wandering around, throw corpses at it
>     (tripe rations work best -- otherwise make sure the corpse is fresh
>      and something dogs/cats usually eat).

> 2 - Use a spell/scroll of taming to tame some hostile monster.

> 3 - Get turned into a were-something, and use #monster to summon
>     more "brethren".  While pet rats may be too wimpy to be useful,
>     you can get them to wander over a polymorph trap (or a zap them
>     with a wand of polymorph), and they could turn something really
>     useful (like a pet leprechaun on a level with a temple priest).
>     On the other hand, they sometime turn into something even more
>     useless (I've had pet mimics and pet mold/fungi).

4 - Drink from a fountain.  After two or three tries you will probably
    get polymorphed, usually into something pretty buff.  In one game
    I got 'morphed to a serpent, so I did #sit about 3 times, and
    hatched some baby serpents (who stayed that way when I changed back).

    Warning:  don't get up off that pile of eggs while Fido is around,
    'cause he'll eat them!  (Or kill him first.)

